# Raw broker exports are hash-pinned. Git must not touch a single byte.
#
# Without this, a clone on Windows with core.autocrlf=true rewrites LF to CRLF
# on checkout, every byte after the first line shifts, and the SHA-256 recorded
# in src/data/raw.py stops matching a file nobody edited. The guard would fire
# on a machine difference and read as data corruption, which is the worst
# possible failure for a check whose entire job is to detect data corruption.
#
# -text disables all end-of-line conversion in both directions.
data/raw/*.csv -text
data/raw/*.sha256 -text

# Same reasoning: the calendar is hashed byte-for-byte by
# src/data/calendar.py, so its line endings are load-bearing.
calendar/*.yaml -text
